Error handling: exact backoff schedule, selective retries, and re-raising the last failure.
-- task.json --
{
  "id": "retry-backoff",
  "title": "Add exponential backoff to retry",
  "category": "error-handling",
  "objective": "retry hides failures: when every attempt fails it returns None, and it waits a fixed delay even after the last attempt. Rework it to back off exponentially, retry only the exceptions the caller names, and re-raise the last failure.",
  "acceptance": [
    "The signature is retry(func, attempts=3, base_delay=0.1, max_delay=2.0, retry_on=(Exception,), sleep=time.sleep), and it returns func()'s result as soon as a call succeeds.",
    "Only exceptions that are instances of retry_on are retried; any other exception propagates immediately without sleeping.",
    "Before retry number k (k = 1, 2, ...) it calls sleep(min(max_delay, base_delay * 2 ** (k - 1))), and it never sleeps after the final attempt.",
    "When every attempt fails it re-raises the last exception object.",
    "attempts below 1, a negative base_delay, or max_delay below base_delay raises ValueError before func is called."
  ],
  "paths": ["netutil/**", "tests/test_retry.py"],
  "verify": [["python3", "-m", "unittest", "-q", "tests.test_retry"]],
  "hidden": [["python3", "-m", "unittest", "-q", "_l7_hidden.test_retry"]],
  "forbidden": {}
}
